Player: This Atomon looks different from the others I've seen.

Player: It seems to keep the same shape.

Player: Even when it moves around, its form doesn't change.

Player: It also doesn't seem to spread out or fill the space around it.

Player: So... it seems to have both a definite shape and a definite volume.

Player: But what is the phase of this Iron Atomon?

- Solid
  Player: Hhmmm, I got it! Since Iron keeps both a definite shape and a definite volume its Solid.

- Liquid
  Player: Not quite. A liquid has a definite volume, but it takes the shape of its container. This Iron Atomon keeps its own shape.

- Gas
  Player: Not quite. A gas does not have a definite shape or volume and tends to spread out to fill the space available.

Player: Then the Iron Atomon is a solid.

Player: Its shape stays the same, and its volume stays the same.

[signal arg="quest_notify:quest_chain_002_01:observe_iron"]

Player: I think I understand.